From: Stained Glass OS <ke7oxh@gmail.com>
Subject: [PATCH] mmdevapi: no session volume watch without an audio driver (9558)

9416's watch of the sound server's mixer (session volumes, and 9419's
default device changes) starts with the first IMMNotificationClient a
program registers. With no driver loaded -- the sound server cannot be
reached, or "no driver" chosen -- its thread started the driver's main
loop anyway: the unix call into the missing driver failed its assert,
and the thread waited for good for the loop to start, holding the
sessions lock. A program that listens for device changes at start
(Steam does) hung with it.

Now the watch starts only when a driver is loaded, as Windows' audio
service is simply absent then.

Gate: test/nodriver-gate.sh (audio drivers disabled). Mutant
SG_MUTANT_WATCH_WITHOUT_DRIVER (mmdevapi/session.c).
---
--- a/dlls/mmdevapi/session.c
+++ b/dlls/mmdevapi/session.c
@@ -218,6 +218,14 @@
 #ifdef SG_MUTANT_PULSE_NO_MIXER_VOLUME
     return;
 #endif
+#ifndef SG_MUTANT_WATCH_WITHOUT_DRIVER
+    /* Stained Glass OS (wine-sg 9558): no sound server reached, no driver
+     * loaded -- nothing to watch. Started anyway, the watch's main loop asserted
+     * in the missing driver and its thread waited for good holding the sessions
+     * lock: a program listening for device changes (Steam at start) hung */
+    if (!drvs.module_unixlib)
+        return;
+#endif
     if (InterlockedCompareExchange(&started, 1, 0))
         return;
     /* the thread waits in the driver for good: the module stays */
